  "body": "Imagine a morning swim before the day begins, children laughing in the pool after school, and friends staying for one more conversation as evening settles in. At 20 Springcombe Road, there is room for everything that makes life feel full—and time to enjoy it.\r\n\r\nWith elevated sea views and St Heliers Beach and village close by, this luxury family home in Auckland’s Eastern Bays brings coastal living and city convenience together. Space, privacy and a full rebuild completed in 2021 create a home ready to enjoy, with room to work, recharge and bring generations together.\r\n\r\nThe approximately 750 sq m residence occupies 1,002 sq m of land, more or less. A timeless weatherboard façade gives way to generous contemporary interiors, where a prized north-facing orientation and expansive glazing welcome natural light and views towards Rangitoto Island. The substantial work is complete; your next chapter can begin.\r\n\r\nThe heated swimming pool is the centre of summer life. Alongside it, a spa and beautifully appointed pool house invite leisurely lunches and celebrations that stretch into the evening. Opening on two sides, the pool house connects with the lawn and pool, keeping everyone part of the occasion, whether swimming, playing or relaxing with friends.\r\n\r\nSunrise yoga, a workout in the home gym and fitness studio, or an evening in the spa: wellbeing finds a natural place in your routine. Beyond the gate, St Heliers Beach, coastal walks and village cafés bring the pleasures of beachside living into every day.\r\n\r\nThe Morgan Cronin-designed kitchen brings everyone together, from breakfast before school to dinner with friends. A joint runner-up for the 2022 NKBA Supreme Kitchen Design Award, it is complemented by a butler’s pantry and two additional kitchens on the lower level and in the pool house, making everyday meals and larger gatherings equally easy.\r\n\r\nFive bedrooms, six bathrooms and multiple living areas offer flexibility for growing and multigenerational families. Grandparents can stay, teenagers can find independence, and guests can settle in comfortably. The additional kitchens support different routines, with options for shared living and greater autonomy within the home.\r\n\r\nQuiet places accommodate work and study, while the media room and outdoor spaces provide room to play and reconnect. Privately positioned, the primary suite offers elevated sea views, generous dressing, a refined en suite and covered outdoor living—a peaceful retreat at either end of the day.\r\n\r\nQuality runs deeper than the finishes. Significant structural engineering underpins the full rebuild, reflecting the care invested throughout. Integrated smart home technology adds everyday comfort and convenience to a residence of enduring substance.\r\n\r\nThis established St Heliers address places you in excellent company, surrounded by distinguished coastal homes and within easy reach of some of Auckland’s most prestigious schools. With Auckland CBD approximately 10 kilometres away, village cafés close by and the waterfront part of daily life, this Eastern Bays setting brings coastal enjoyment and city convenience together.\r\n\r\nFor buyers seeking a luxury Auckland home with sea views, private wellness amenities and room for every generation, 20 Springcombe Road offers a compelling opportunity to move straight into the life you want.\r\n\r\nMake this the summer you come home to St Heliers.\r\n\r\nPrivate viewings by appointment. Contact us for further information and to discuss settlement options for summer.\r\n\r\nKelly Brown\r\n+64 21 471 661 | kelly.brown@nzsir.com\r\n\r\nJackie Parker\r\n+64 21 505 520 | jackie.parker@nzsir.com\r\n\r\nImportant: This property may be marketed as suitable for overseas purchasers. However, this does not constitute confirmation of eligibility, approval, or suitability for any individual buyer. All overseas purchasers remain subject to New Zealand’s overseas investment laws, including the Overseas Investment Act 2005.",
